## 1. User Stories

> Format: "As a [role], I want [action] so that [benefit]."

| Story ID | User Story | Linked FR | Acceptance Criteria | Priority |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| US-001 | As a **student**, I want to search for books by title, author, or ISBN so that I can quickly find resources I need. | FR-02 / UC02 | Results in under 2 seconds; availability shown; filters work without page reload. | High |
| US-002 | As a **student**, I want to register and log in with my university email so that my account is linked to my institution. | FR-01 / UC01 | Non-university emails blocked; JWT issued on login; lockout after 5 failed attempts. | High |
| US-003 | As a **student**, I want to borrow or reserve a book online so that I do not have to visit the library in person. | FR-03 / UC03 | Loan created with 14-day due date; inventory updated; confirmation email within 60 seconds. | High |
| US-004 | As a **student**, I want to view my personal dashboard so that I can see my loans, due dates, and overdue notices. | FR-04 / UC04 | Dashboard loads in under 2 seconds; items due within 3 days highlighted in red. | High |
| US-005 | As a **student**, I want personalized book recommendations so that I can discover resources relevant to my course. | FR-05 / UC05 | At least 10 recommendations shown; updated every 24 hours; new students get defaults within 1 hour. | Medium |
| US-006 | As a **librarian**, I want to add, edit, and delete catalogue resources so that the library inventory stays accurate. | FR-06 / UC06 | New resources indexed within 30 seconds; ISBN validated; deletion blocked if active loans exist. | High |
| US-007 | As a **student**, I want automated email reminders before my book is due so that I can return it on time. | FR-07 / UC07 | Emails sent 3 days before, on, and 1 day after due date; includes title, due date, and dashboard link. | High |
| US-008 | As an **administrator**, I want to generate and export usage reports so that I can make data-driven procurement decisions. | FR-08 / UC08 | Filterable by date and department; PDF/CSV export within 10 seconds. | Medium |
| US-009 | As an **external developer**, I want a versioned REST API with OpenAPI docs so that I can integrate library features into the university portal. | FR-09 / UC09 | Swagger UI at /api/v1/docs; correct HTTP status codes; sandbox available 24/7. | Medium |
| US-010 | As an **IT administrator**, I want role-based access control so that each role only accesses relevant features. | FR-10 / UC10 | Students blocked from admin endpoints; unauthorized requests return HTTP 403; changes audit-logged. | High |
| US-011 | As a **student**, I want to save resources to a reading list so that I can track books I want to read later. | FR-11 / UC11 | Saved in 1 click; up to 10 collections; persists across devices. | Low |
| US-012 | As a **student with a disability**, I want a keyboard-navigable interface so that I can use the system independently. | FR-12 / UC04 | Lighthouse score over 95; all elements reachable by keyboard; ARIA live regions work. | High |
| US-013 | As a **system administrator**, I want all data encrypted with AES-256 over TLS so that POPIA compliance is maintained. | NFR-09 | No plaintext personal data in DB; SSL Labs Grade A; TLS on all endpoints. | High |
| US-014 | As a **librarian**, I want to bulk import resources from CSV so that I can add large acquisitions quickly. | FR-06 / UC06a | Up to 1,000 rows processed; invalid rows flagged; valid records indexed within 60 seconds. | Medium |

