## 2. Product Backlog

> Prioritized using MoSCoW. Effort uses Fibonacci story points (1, 2, 3, 5, 8).

| Story ID | Summary | MoSCoW | Story Points | Dependencies |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| US-002 | Student registration and login | Must-have | 3 | None |
| US-010 | Role-based access control | Must-have | 3 | US-002 |
| US-013 | AES-256 encryption and TLS | Must-have | 2 | US-002 |
| US-001 | Search library catalogue | Must-have | 5 | US-002 |
| US-003 | Borrow and reserve a book | Must-have | 5 | US-001, US-002 |
| US-004 | Student personal dashboard | Must-have | 5 | US-002, US-003 |
| US-006 | Librarian catalogue management | Must-have | 5 | US-010 |
| US-007 | Automated overdue notifications | Must-have | 3 | US-003 |
| US-012 | Accessible interface (WCAG 2.1 AA) | Must-have | 3 | US-001, US-004 |
| US-005 | Personalized recommendations | Should-have | 8 | US-001, US-003 |
| US-008 | Usage reports and analytics | Should-have | 5 | US-003, US-006 |
| US-009 | REST API for external integration | Should-have | 5 | US-002, US-001 |
| US-014 | Bulk CSV import for librarians | Should-have | 3 | US-006 |
| US-011 | Student reading list | Could-have | 2 | US-001, US-002 |

### Prioritization Justification

Must-have stories form the MVP: authentication, RBAC, encryption, search, borrowing, dashboard, catalogue management, notifications, and accessibility. These map directly to the highest-priority stakeholder success metrics from STAKEHOLDERS.md. Without these, SALAS cannot function as a library system.

Should-have stories deliver significant value but can be deferred to Sprint 2 and 3 without blocking the MVP. Could-have stories are low-effort enhancements that improve the experience but are not required for core functionality.

